adjudication.rationale:
In the new `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` handler, the auth check is:

```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET) {
  return res.status(403)
}
```

If `CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is unset at runtime (so `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is `undefined`) and the request also omits the header (so `req.headers[...]` is `undefined`), the comparison evaluates to `false` (`undefined !== undefined`), so the request is incorrectly allowed through. After that, the caller controls `userId`, `appSlug`, and `keys`, and the code will update or create credentials for that arbitrary `userId` without any additional user-scoping/authorization checks in this diff. The only remaining gate is `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED`, whose behavior is outside the diff, so the exploitability depends on how that constant is set, but the fail-open behavior on missing secret is directly verifiable in the diff.
